---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Terminal from "../../components/Terminal.astro";
import { INSTALL_SH } from "../../data/site";

const init = `coding.sh init --dry-run              # print every file edit, write nothing
coding.sh init                        # install hooks into every detected agent
coding.sh init --agent claude-code    # or just one`;
const explore = `coding.sh sessions --since 7d         # newest first
coding.sh show latest                 # one session's timeline
coding.sh search 'flaky test'         # full text over prompts, replies, tool calls
coding.sh ui                          # local viewer on 127.0.0.1:4319`;
const backfill = `coding.sh ingest --backfill --since 30d`;
const wrap = `coding.sh run -- aider --message 'fix the failing test'
coding.sh run --agent my-agent -- ./my-agent --task 42`;

const esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
const m = (s: string) => `<span class="t-muted">${esc(s)}</span>`;
const t = (s: string) => `<span class="t-text">${esc(s)}</span>`;
const SHOW = [
  `${m("$")} ${t("coding.sh show latest")}`,
  t("add() returns the wrong result, fix it"),
  `  ${m("Session ")}      22222222-2222-3333-4444-555555555555`,
  `  ${m("Agent   ")}      claude-code  claude-sonnet-4-5`,
  `  ${m("Repo    ")}      ~/acme/calc`,
  `  ${m("Turns   ")}      1, 2 tool calls, 0 files changed`,
  `  ${m("Latency ")}      tools 57ms (p95 29ms)`,
  "",
  `    ${m("+0ms")}  session.start`,
  `   ${m("+29ms")}  user        add() returns the wrong result, fix it`,
  `   ${m("+85ms")}  tool        Read ~/acme/calc/add.js  ok 28ms`,
  `  ${m("+143ms")}  tool        Bash node test.js  ok 29ms`,
  `  ${m("+173ms")}  turn.end`,
].join("\n");
---

<DocsLayout>
  <Code code={INSTALL_SH} />
  <p>
    That installs the CLI, runs <code>init</code> and opens the viewer. Other ways to install are on <a href="/docs/install">Install</a>. For
    agent frameworks rather than coding agents, see <a href="/docs/otel">OpenTelemetry</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="init">1. Install the hooks</h2>
  <p>
    <code>init</code> detects the agents on your machine and adds one hook command to each agent's config. Every file it edits is backed up to
    <code>~/.coding.sh/backups</code> first, and its entries are marked so <code>uninstall</code> removes only them.
  </p>
  <Code code={init} />
  <p>
    <code>--scope project</code> writes to the repository's agent config (for example <code>.claude/settings.json</code>) instead of your user
    config.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Codex:</strong> Codex runs a new hook only after you trust it. Open Codex and approve the coding.sh entries with
      <code>/hooks</code>. coding.sh never writes trust state for you; <code>doctor</code> tells you when hooks are still untrusted.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="use">2. Use your agent as usual</h2>
  <p>
    Each hook appends one line to <code>~/.coding.sh/spool</code> and exits 0. It makes no network calls and prints nothing, because several
    agents read hook output as a decision or as text for the model. If capture fails, the failure goes to <code>spool/errors.log</code> and
    the agent carries on.
  </p>

  <h2 id="explore">3. Look at what was captured</h2>
  <p>Read commands ingest the spool first, so a session shows up as soon as its events are written.</p>
  <Code code={explore} />
  <Terminal title="~/acme/calc" label="Output of coding.sh show latest">
    <pre set:html={SHOW} />
  </Terminal>
  <p>
    Subagents are child sessions: <code>sessions --subagents</code> lists them, and <code>show</code> places them on the parent's timeline.
    Every command takes <code>--json</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="backfill">4. Import past sessions</h2>
  <p>Most agents keep local transcripts. <code>--backfill</code> imports them, so history from before <code>init</code> shows up too. Re-running it inserts nothing new: event ids are deterministic.</p>
  <Code code={backfill} />

  <h2 id="wrap">Agents without hooks</h2>
  <p>
    <code>coding.sh run -- &lt;cmd&gt;</code> works with anything. It snapshots the repository before and after the command, records each changed
    file, and exits with the command's exit code.
  </p>
  <Code code={wrap} />

  <h2 id="latency">Model-call latency</h2>
  <p>
    Hooks see tool calls, not model calls. Most adapters recover one <code>llm.call</code> event per model call from the agent's transcript,
    with timing derived from message timestamps. For measured durations and time to first token from Claude Code, turn on its OpenTelemetry
    export and run <code>coding.sh collector</code>: see <a href="/docs/otel#claude-code">Claude Code over OTel</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/agents">Coding agents</a>: what each adapter captures.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/evals">Evals</a>: datasets, graders and paired comparisons.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/cli">CLI reference</a>: every command and flag.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
